    {
        "content": "<p>Does anyone know why theorem b_s works but theorem b_ds not in the following example:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ys</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b_s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b_ds</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">replicate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">xs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">·</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">admit</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- exact ih</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In particular it seems like iota reduction succeeds with simp but not with dsimp and at the same time it succeeds with only dsimp in theorem a. Is some branch optimization at play here that is not simmetrical with respect to the left and right <code>le</code> arguments?</p>",
        "id": 593682038,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1778214822
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What ends up happening is that <code>le</code> has an equation with the assumption that all relevant previous cases don't apply (i.e. something like <code>∀ a, _x = Nat.succ a → _y = Nat.zero → False</code>) and then <code>simp</code> handles these kinds of hypotheses specially in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/819f4549d9bda7c34f1ae185a3353d7dfd1f19a6/src/Lean/Meta/Tactic/Simp/Rewrite.lean#L595\">dischargeEqnThmHypothesis?</a>. This equation is not by <code>rfl</code> though, so it doesn't work with <code>dsimp</code> (or with <code>exact</code>, for that matter).</p>",
        "id": 593784877,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1778245960
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I totally understand that simp will do more and be more flexible than dsimp here, what confused me in particular is that this is a symmetric case where both the <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> arguments could be eliminated based on symmetrical properties (one not being zero and one not being succ) yet dsimp does work in one direction and not in the other.</p>",
        "id": 593927247,
        "sender_full_name": "Plamen Dimitrov",
        "timestamp": 1778298721
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well your <code>le</code> gets desugared into (roughly):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">l₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">::</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">zero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">head₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">succ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">False</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₂</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tail₂</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Notably, we don't reduce to <code>le tail₁ tail₂</code> before reducing <code>head₂</code> to either <code>Nat.zero</code> or <code>Nat.succ _</code>.</p>",
        "id": 594034989,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1778369653
    }
]